          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "अवज्ञा — avajñā — \"contempt\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "गुरोः अवज्ञा न उचिता। guroḥ avajñā na ucitā. Contempt for a teacher is not proper."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A feminine noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "अवज्ञा (avajñā) is built from ava, \"down\", and the root √jñā, \"to know\", the root of जानाति: to think little of; MW gives \"contempt, disesteem, disrespect\" (MW)."
            }
          ]
        },
